    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pine Ridge lies in the Ridge and Valley section of the Appalachian Mountains, surrounded by low ridges and valleys.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pine_Ridge%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pine Ridge’s compact footprint in the Appalachian foothills shows how ridges and valleys guided early settlement along accessible routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pine_ridge_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pine Ridge officially incorporated in 1982, soon after establishing a town hall and holding its first municipal elections.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pine_ridge_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mid‑19th‑century farmers from Georgia and Tennessee settled Pine Ridge, drawn by the fertile valleys of the Appalachian foothills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pine_ridge_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Rugged topography kept large farms out of Pine Ridge, fostering modest family farms and logging operations in its pine‑covered ridges.",
